WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.320
March 1983

2
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.640
Part VII
Every lighthouse has its own light

3
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.440
Pille, it has finally happened!
- What?

4
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.880
Old Nikifor has bit the dust.
- Really?

5
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.720
Why else send the car?
Come, see for yourself. Hurry!

6
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.960
Oh my god...
- Oh my god!

7
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:52.480
Aino's crying next to the stretcher.
Ugh, toes are still twitching!

8
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.480
Perhaps he's not completely dead.
- No, no, believe me, he's done for.

9
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:06.760
They twitch before the rigor mortis.
- He's still a human being.

10
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.360
Was.

11
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.040
He insulted us, though he lived in
a room that's part of our apartment.

12
00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.200
If a person disappears,
their apartment is still left.

13
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.400
It's as simple as that.
- You bloody cynic.

14
00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:02.760
Hello, dear! Awesome news!
I got 2 kg of tangerines.

15
00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:11.320
Oh, wonderful. Come, sit down.
I have even bigger news.

16
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.920
You got 4 kilos?
- Old Nikifor left.

17
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.720
I see.

18
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.640
I'm saving my emotions
for the moment he's really dead.

19
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.840
But he is.
- You said the same thing last time,

20
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:50.400
when it really was Brezhnev.
- Paavo and Pille saw.

21
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.920
Are we really going to get
the whole apartment?

22
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:09.240
I don't know, seems so. Old Nikifor
finally stopped vegetating.

23
00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.080
He wasn't very good at it anyway.

24
00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.560
May he find peace.

25
00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.240
May God bless his soul.
- Yes.

26
00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.800
Perhaps we should bring that Finnish
wallpaper down from the attic?

27
00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:31.120
I don't know, the hag's mourning,
she might completely lose it.

28
00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.000
Let's keep low profile.

29
00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:37.680
True.
- If we meet her,

30
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:44.080
we'll give our condolences and if she
wants to speak, let her go first.

31
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.240
Oh, lord, you gave me such a scare!

32
00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:09.000
What would have become of me
if I'd lost you?

33
00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.520
Come now, mom, the ambulance
came right on time.

34
00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.120
I'll be fine after surgery.

35
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.920
But can you still stay on the force?

36
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.960
Men like me are more valuable
than before, honestly.

37
00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.800
How so?
- They can always count on us.

38
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.520
On decisive moments there's no need
to worry about an appendix.

39
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:49.360
Today is an ordinary weekend day
in Tallinn's emergency room.

40
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.400
We're currently in the neurosurgery
and neurotraumatology ward.

41
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.080
Several patients have been accepted
today,

42
00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:05.720
here we have three people
with brain trauma, all inebriated.

43
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:13.720
I love my woman deeply,
the sea madly and in secrecy.

44
00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:13.520
When I got older, my dad thought
that a sailor...

45
00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:19.560
You? I thought Paavo.
Where is everybody?

46
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.080
Where should I know,
I'm no police!

47
00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.760
Damn it,
I can't listen to the radio like this.

48
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:43.280
What do you want?
- I came to see my family.

49
00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.280
Your family's on the Reepenbahn.
- I hardly know the people there.

50
00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.640
Here, I brought something for you too,
dear father-in-law.

51
00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:58.520
You have your face on the cigar case?
- No, these are cigarillos.

52
00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:01.880
First of all,
I'm content with our cigarettes.

53
00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.520
Secondly, I'm not your
father-in-law.

54
00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:08.320
Well, according to the papers...
- Forget the papers!

55
00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:16.080
I've forgiven you that you helped
my daughter start her red career.

56
00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:23.240
But I'll never forgive you cheating
on her with those harbor harlots!

57
00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.880
Come now, that's all in the past.
- Why should I believe a man

58
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.960
who's apparently a living jammer?
How gullible do you think I am?

59
00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:38.000
I hoped I could have a serious talk
with you, but apparently not.

60
00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:44.840
I could have gone to our militsiya and
told the fool what you're listening to.

61
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.560
But I'm not going to descend to that.
- Go ahead, you bloody snitch!

62
00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:52.720
And take him more of those things
you got him for Christmas!

63
00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:57.280
I've changed my mind!
I'll never forgive you that

64
00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.800
you made my daughter into a communist.

65
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.640
I forgive nothing,
you shitty conformist!

66
00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.760
I'm going to leave now,
but I'll be back.

67
00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:16.520
I'll come back to my legal home,
to meet my legal wife and kids,

68
00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.600
and I want you, old fart,
out of this house.

69
00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:25.440
Big tough guy.
Bloody nihilist!

70
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.400
Good day, comrade neighbor!
- Hello!

71
00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:51.600
I only wanted to say, that I'm sorry
that things went like they did.

72
00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:55.560
What things?
- The ambulance came and... over.

73
00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.120
The kids saw it this morning.

74
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.520
We're very sorry.

75
00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.520
Well, thank you.

76
00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.760
If it was meant to happen
then what can we do.

77
00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:18.760
Did he suffer?
- Yes, at first, but it's over now.

78
00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.200
Oh well.

79
00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:26.840
That's how the human beings are made.
It can only happen once.

80
00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:33.920
Wise words, wise words.
If you need anything,

81
00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.800
don't hesitate to ask.

82
00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.320
I won't. I'll let you know!

83
00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:53.920
I have seen all kinds of people,
but she is a special character.

84
00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.480
Aino's as much human as Vigri.

85
00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.600
Vigri.
Vigri was the mascot of

86
00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.040
Moscow 1980 Olympic Games'
competitive sailing events,

87
00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.480
which were held in Tallinn.
Produced in toy factory Polümeer.

88
00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.040
Initially, mascot's eyes were designed
to be blue, black and white,

89
00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.440
but Moscow forbade the idea and
ordered blue color to be removed.

90
00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:19.440
What?

91
00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:22.840
I can never tell whether she is
a human or a beast.

92
00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:26.480
No, I mean that she seemed happy.

93
00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:33.440
Like a wart had been removed.
- What about your low profile?

94
00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:37.320
I didn't say anything specific,
gave my condolences.

95
00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:41.800
I swear, if you screw this up again...

96
00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.240
Then the soldier has died in vain.

97
00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.040
Hello!

98
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.560
Where are you calling from?

99
00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:53.840
I see.

100
00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:58.440
No, no, we're their neighbors,
we have a parallel phone.

101
00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.880
What? Are you quite sure?

102
00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.920
Okay, I'll tell her.

103
00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:13.960
Yes, thank you.
Good bye.

104
00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:17.440
Oh dear god have mercy...
- What happened?

105
00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.640
It was for Aino,
called from the hospital.

106
00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.960
And?

107
00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:37.840
Asked me to tell Aino that when she
goes to the hospital to visit her son,

108
00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:44.680
she should bring his radio, whistle
and staff.

109
00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:49.720
He'll be out in few days, but he's
missing his work a lot.

110
00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:53.480
Did something happen to the militsiya?
Is something wrong?

111
00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:59.800
What are you sewing here, a dress
or something else?

112
00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:04.760
Tell me about the cop.
- I'm just a messenger.

113
00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:11.840
The one taken away this morning,
it was Jüri Kessner, not Nikifor.

114
00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.400
Ruptured appendix...

115
00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:16.600
You did it again!

116
00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.280
I did nothing!

117
00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.640
Pille ja Paavo did,
I mean saw...

118
00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:36.440
Now we're in Kalev sweets factory's
newest building - the bubblegum house.

119
00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:47.240
We're making our chewing gum from
French or Italian chewing gum

120
00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:51.200
and French bubblegum.

121
00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:57.040
Right now you're producing only
peppermint and Cola flavored gum.

122
00:12:57.520 --> 00:13:01.960
In few month's time,
after tests are done,

123
00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.400
we'll start making
coffee flavored gum too.

124
00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:08.800
Hey, you don't happen to have
a leftover pack of Jenkki?

125
00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.880
What's this, a communist youth
craves Finnish chewing gum?

126
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:14.040
No! A girl at school has two
of the same Dallas' stickers

127
00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:19.680
and I could swap with her.
- Good! But I'm sorry, I'm all out.

128
00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.720
But I bet you'll get you gum
in the evening, dad's coming again!

129
00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.480
How do you know?
- He's already been here,

130
00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.840
but we were out.
- What makes you think that?

131
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.360
It's elementary -
the room's full of sea smell

132
00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:33.600
and there was an empty Malboro
pack under a bush outside.

133
00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.600
Nobody nearby smokes that.
- Okay.

134
00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.920
But perhaps your friend Alex has some?
- Has what?

135
00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.600
Western chud.

136
00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:50.160
Foreign chewing gum.
Modern chewing gum was invented

137
00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:54.960
in 1850 by John B. Curtis, but people
in the Soviet Union didn't hear

138
00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.360
about it for another hundred years.

139
00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:03.080
Kalev's gum had been invented
by the 80's, but it was monochrome.

140
00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:08.000
Aren't you listening to me?
Dad will bring us

141
00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:11.560
all kinds of goodies in the evening.
- I don't want Villem's things.

142
00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.720
I'd rather live without the sticker.

143
00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.080
Why are you calling dad Villem
all of a sudden?

144
00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:23.240
He's not a proper father!
- Are you nuts?

145
00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.000
A dad who comes to see his kids
once in a blue moon,

146
00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.200
and then tries to buy them off with
rarities.

147
00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.880
When was the last time you two
did something together?

148
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:35.200
At the end of the year,
when I had problems with...

149
00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:39.080
stuff you're too young for.

150
00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:43.760
Wasn't it Ats who saved you from
that jam with porno magazine?

151
00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.360
Playboy's not porno.
- What ever.

152
00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.520
Okay, I had to use a double.

153
00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:53.160
And wasn't it Ats, who helped you
print T-shirts?

154
00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.760
And freed your hand when you were
trying to fish out a lighter

155
00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.440
and got stuck in the toilet bowl?

156
00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:02.480
And he got you into the technical
institute, though you repeated

157
00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:06.040
the last high school grade twice.
It was all Ats!

158
00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:09.680
Fine! But it's not our dad's fault

159
00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:13.320
that his job doesn't let him
stay at home all the time.

160
00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.000
You know what you sell yourself for!

161
00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:19.160
My father, real father is Villem.

162
00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:24.600
And if you don't like his chewwy,

163
00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.320
make your own!
- How?

164
00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:29.280
Like all prole kids do!
- How?

165
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:36.080
Take our chewing gum and mix it with
ground up cores of colored pencils.

166
00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.960
How did you know?
Have you tried to do that?

167
00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:42.960
Sometimes I pinch some from you.
Like you take mom's Malboro

168
00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.680
that she gets from Villem.
- Will you help me do it?

169
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.720
Sure, why not.
- Cheap popularity!

170
00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:56.800
Hello! Look who's home!
- Hi, dad!

171
00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.040
Come here!

172
00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.680
Well, daughter, come here!
- No!

173
00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:23.400
What's up, are you in bad mood?
We'll fix that right away!

174
00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:29.280
I bet some Coke will help,
catch!

175
00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:33.960
Here, throw it in the laundry.
A cabby wanted to buy it from me!

176
00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:38.200
Come, boy, look what your old man
got you!

177
00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:44.720
Hey, sea dog!
- What is it, landman?

178
00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:51.160
I should tell you few things,
so you'd make a fool of yourself.

179
00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.640
Nikifor died yesterday.

180
00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:02.880
So don't say anything stupid
in front of Aino. Be polite, and such.

181
00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.640
I see.

182
00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:14.240
Kids, go to your room,
the men have to talk.

183
00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:17.000
I'm a man too.
- Go now, take the bag.

184
00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:20.680
I'm not leaving the room.
- It won't take long.

185
00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.960
Keep your hands off mom's cigarettes!
- Dad!

186
00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:34.080
You, little man with a small dick
and big bright ideas,

187
00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:38.080
do you think I can't see through you?
- I beg your pardon?

188
00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:44.000
I know you're after my wife
and this apartment,

189
00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.480
especially the neighbor's share.

190
00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.240
The place is in your name,
Sirje as well.

191
00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.520
And will stay so!

192
00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:57.720
Soon we'll be living here together,
me, Sirje and the kids.

193
00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:03.960
But you, Casanova, will have to find
yourself a new place to stay at.

194
00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:07.080
Does Sirje know about this?

195
00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:10.200
She will soon.

196
00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:17.520
Fine, that's that then.
- You give up this easily?

197
00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:20.520
What else can I do?

198
00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.440
Nothing much, really.

199
00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.720
You could at least tell the hag
that you're sorry for her loss.

200
00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:37.360
You care as much for her feelings
as I adore Soviet jeans.

201
00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.960
I bet on a carton of Malboro
that you're after her apartment.

202
00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.200
You won't get away with that!

203
00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:59.240
Hello, Sirje!
- Ats, dear, I got tickets to

204
00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.600
Sofia Rotaru's concert on Saturday.

205
00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:08.760
Sofia Rotaru.
Hugely popular Ukrainian-Moldovan

206
00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:13.000
pop singer in the 1980's Soviet Union.
USSR's People's Artist.

207
00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.360
In 2000, she was named the

208
00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:20.400
Best Ukrainian Pop Singer
of the Twentieth Century.

209
00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.600
She was as famous as
Estonian Jaak Joala.

210
00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:29.400
Rotaru? Two months ago I saw
ABBA in Sweden.

211
00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:32.240
On a TV in a bar.
- No, in real life.

212
00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:35.840
Our bus went past Stockholm's TV house
and they were going in.

213
00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.760
Oh, they're so cool, not like
that cow Rotaru.

214
00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:42.440
What are you doing here again?
- I came to see my family.

215
00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.840
Actually, I need to speak with you.

216
00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:48.760
Make it quick.

217
00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.240
Perhaps...

218
00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:54.920
Ats!

219
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:05.760
Okay, fine. He's a grown man
has chest hair and everything.

220
00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:20.840
Sirje, I think we should start over.
You have no idea how much I miss you.

221
00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:25.040
See, I have this with me always.

222
00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:29.240
Sprinkle it on a pillow

223
00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:34.000
and imagine that you're next to me.
- Don't your foreign girlfriends

224
00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:41.200
mind the smell of a cheap perfume?
- I've never ever... compared you

225
00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:45.240
with a one night stand.
I can't even remember their faces.

226
00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.600
No-one could remember that many.
- The KGB for instance...

227
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.400
What?
- Nothing.

228
00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.800
Do you yourself believe what
you're saying?

229
00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.480
Yes, and to prove that...

230
00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:01.960
Prove what?

231
00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:08.240
That I love you.
Now that Nikifor's gone to his

232
00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:13.480
trench pals,
the whole apartment will be ours.

233
00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.600
I'm willing to give
it all to you, officially.

234
00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:19.080
Wait, Nikifor's...

235
00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:23.920
And that idiot, who's standing there

236
00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.600
and rubbing his mustache,
his time will be over too,

237
00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.520
and we will be together again.

238
00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:31.720
Are you saying that you want to

239
00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:36.880
give the apartment to me?
- Yes! I'll do anything for you!

240
00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:43.040
What's that stale stench here,
has something gone bad?

241
00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:45.000
Oh, you're here again!
Hello!

242
00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:46.040
Hello!

243
00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:49.120
"17 Moments of Spring" is on!
Aren't you watching it?

244
00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.480
Aino, let's step to the hall,
I'd like to talk to you.

245
00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:54.960
Right now?

246
00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:10.160
Dear comrade Aino.

247
00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:20.720
I can hardly speak, I'm so sorry.

248
00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:24.520
Yes, be quick.
I want to go watch the TV.

249
00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:31.480
To think, what a hero.
And then all of a sudden...

250
00:22:31.640 --> 00:22:35.200
I hope he wasn't in pain.
- There's nothing to say,

251
00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:40.560
it's all over.
- And the funeral?

252
00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:47.920
What funeral? Comrade,
have you lost your mind?

253
00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:51.680
It was only his appendix.
He'll be out tomorrow.

254
00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:58.760
I thought that in his age
it would've been normal.

255
00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:02.840
His age?
My son is a lot younger than you

256
00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:08.080
and will probably live longer too,
considering his sober lifestyle.

257
00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.000
Your son?
- You've been drinking absinthe again?

258
00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.360
But... what about Nikifor?
How's he?

259
00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:16.760
Comrade Captain,
do you know the statue Russalka?

260
00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.040
Yes, what about it?

261
00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:23.200
Has been standing by the sea for
decades, not moving or changing.

262
00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:26.880
Nikifor's the same. No changes.

263
00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:36.960
Every lighthouse has its own light.

264
00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:42.080
Nikifor, dear!
Dear god!

265
00:24:44.720 --> 00:24:47.240
I fooled you, didn't you?
